      'Method (course convention). Vary one weight wₖ from its base value and rescale the others in proportion so that the weights still sum to one. Then every alternative’s total is a straight line in wₖ: V_a(w) = w · v_ak + (1 − w) · S_a, where S_a = (V_a − wₖ v_ak) / (1 − wₖ) is the alternative’s value on the other criteria, renormalised. Two alternatives a and b tie where w* = (S_b − S_a) / ((v_ak − S_a) − (v_bk − S_b)). Plotting these lines is SEBoK’s line diagram for swing-weight sensitivity (R18 p.472). The proportional-rescaling rule is not stated in R18; it is the convention L7 uses so that results are comparable between teams.',
